  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting national cohesion peace consolidation and youths&#x2019; transformation with employability skills</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is proposed to have a four-month project cost-extension (November 2024 to February 2025) aimed at facilitating the successful completion of critical components of the peace-building and national cohesion project initiated in November 2023. This is to close the training gaps of the youths and successfully transition the youths supported.
The proposed project is designed specifically to consolidate the political intolerance and fragile peace triggered by the national political activities rooted in the political power desire. The proposed project will further integrate livelihoods approach specifically targeting youths in the informal setting primarily use for political gains to orchestrate civil unrest and political violence. 
The project is embedded with three prone intentions which are:
 * Strengthen faith leaders and youths&#x2019; capacities to enhance their constructive engagements with state actors, non-state actors and communities on peace mediation and reconciliation.
 * Facilitate coordination among state and non-state actors to identify election conflict drivers, grievances, and inclusive approaches to address them.
 * Transformative strategy for youths in the informal setting/sector through the integration of resilience livelihoods thereby forestalling self-reliance and employability. 
The entire project concept is linked to CAFOD&#x2019;s programme strategy  which include:
 * Improved Governance and
 * Resilience Livelihood.
The proposed project will play positive role in building peace in local communities and nationwide which resonate with CRS&#x2019; Education for a Culture of Peace  programme areas of intervention.
The entire project will be implemented jointly by the two partners (Inter Religious Council of Sierra Leone and Future View Salone) with funding support from CAFOD and CRS. However, IRCSL is the Lead Applicant and bears the responsibility of accountability to CAFOD and CRS.</narrative>
  </description>
